### Telemetry Packet Generation Sketch

This sketch reads simulated rover telemetry metrics and formats them into a clean, delimited telemetry packet transmitted out the serial port every 500 milliseconds.

```cpp
// Monster Lab - Telemetry Stream Formatter
unsigned long lastTelemetryTime = 0;
const unsigned long TELEMETRY_INTERVAL = 500; // 500ms update rate
unsigned long packetSequence = 0;

void setup() {
  Serial.begin(9600); // 9600 baud serial connection
  while (!Serial) { ; } // Wait for serial connection
  Serial.println("# MONSTER LAB ROBOT TELEMETRY INITIALIZED");
}

void loop() {
  unsigned long currentMillis = millis();

  // Non-blocking timer: send telemetry at regular intervals
  if (currentMillis - lastTelemetryTime >= TELEMETRY_INTERVAL) {
    lastTelemetryTime = currentMillis;
    packetSequence++;

    // Simulate reading robot telemetry metrics
    int batteryLevel = 88;       // Battery charge percentage (%)
    int distanceObstacle = 145;  // Ultrasonic distance (cm)
    float boardTemp = 24.5;      // Microcontroller temperature (C)

    // Construct standardized delimited telemetry frame
    Serial.print("$TLM,");
    Serial.print(packetSequence);
    Serial.print(",BAT:");
    Serial.print(batteryLevel);
    Serial.print(",DIST:");
    Serial.print(distanceObstacle);
    Serial.print(",TEMP:");
    Serial.print(boardTemp, 1);
    Serial.println("*END"); // println automatically appends \r\n
  }
}
```

### Code Breakdown:
1. **Non-blocking Timing (`millis()`):** Never use `delay()` in telemetry systems. `delay()` stops the CPU from processing incoming safety commands!
2. **Frame Identifier (`$TLM`):** Distinguishes valid telemetry packets from random electrical noise.
3. **Delimiter Commas (`,`):** Allows receiving software to split fields cleanly.
4. **Packet Terminator (`println()`):** Appends `\r\n` to signal to the receiving dashboard that a complete packet has landed.
